-- title:
--   Candidate finite Mobius table through 1200000 — data block 3
-- statement:
--   Packed candidate values for $\mu(n)$ on $0\le n<1200001$, together with small prime-factor witnesses, in blocks of 32. This is the fixed data for a finite arithmetic certificate. The data declaration alone does not assert equality with the Möbius function: every block of factor and recurrence checks must be proved separately. This module contains table blocks 16 through 23, each covering up to 8192 consecutive integer positions. It is pure candidate data; correctness is a separate theorem obligation.
-- source:
--   Original finite arithmetic data toward O. Ramare, From explicit estimates for primes to explicit estimates for the Mobius function, Acta Arithmetica 157 (2013), section 9, Lemma 9.1. https://www.impan.pl/shop/en/publication/transaction/download/product/82991. Generated by an exact integer linear sieve; correctness is a separate kernel-checked certificate obligation. Written by Codex.

